cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
title: "Quantization Damage Lives in the Tail: domain-dependent divergence in a 27B coding model, and what task benchmarks can and cannot bound"
abstract: >-
  A measurement study of Qwen3.8-27B across four Unsloth GGUF quantizations on two
  consumer 16 GB GPUs. Reports that quantization damage to code is concentrated in
  the tail of the token distribution, that three independent classes of task
  benchmark bound rather than resolve the effect, and the systems findings that
  determine a long-context deployment on this class of hardware.
type: dataset
license: CC-BY-4.0
